397 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Wheels Compared to the qualifiers' car \(17.7 mm wide wheels\), the new design features 13.1 mm front wheels and 17.1 mm rear wheels. The central part of each wheel is fixed to reduce turbulence caused by the rotating wheel. Due to rule constraints \(Pirelli sticker placement\), we slightly changed our ideas and added a smooth side surface on the wheel for outer stickers, while inner stickers are applied to the central hub. The use of smaller wheels significantly reduced air resistance and improved aerodynamic efficiency, especially at the front.)
/E (Wheels Compared to the qualifiers' car \(17.7 mm wide wheels\), the new design features 13.1 mm front wheels and 17.1 mm rear wheels. The central part of each wheel is fixed to reduce turbulence caused by the rotating wheel. Due to rule constraints \(Pirelli sticker placement\), we slightly changed our ideas and added a smooth side surface on the wheel for outer stickers, while inner stickers are applied to the central hub. The use of smaller wheels significantly reduced air resistance and improved aerodynamic efficiency, especially at the front.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
